$\text{SO}_3$: $0$ $\text{S}-\text{S}$ bonds;
$\text{S}_2\text{O}_3^{2-}$ (thiosulphate): $1$ $\text{S}=\text{S}$ bond;
$\text{S}_2\text{O}_6^{2-}$ (dithionate): $1$ $\text{S}-\text{S}$ bond;
$\text{S}_2\text{O}_8^{2-}$ (peroxodisulphate): $0$ $\text{S}-\text{S}$ bonds (contains a peroxo $-\text{O}-\text{O}-$ linkage).
Thus, the numbers of $\text{S}-\text{S}$ bonds are $0, 1, 1, 0$.

$\text{CaF}_2 + \text{H}_2\text{SO}_4 \longrightarrow \text{CaSO}_4 + 2\text{HF}(g)$;
$\text{SiO}_2 + 4\text{HF}(g) \longrightarrow \text{SiF}_4(g) + 2\text{H}_2\text{O}$;
$3\text{SiF}_4 + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \longrightarrow 2\text{H}_2\text{SiF}_6 + \text{SiO}_2$ (official JEE key: C, hydrofluorosilicic acid / hydrated silica suspension).

$\text{XeF}_6 + \text{H}_2\text{O} \longrightarrow \text{XeOF}_4 + 2\text{HF}$;
$2\text{XeF}_6 + \text{SiO}_2 \longrightarrow 2\text{XeOF}_4 + \text{SiF}_4$.
Thus, the common compound $\text{X}$ is $\text{XeOF}_4$.

