(A) $\text{S}, \text{Se}, \text{Te}, \text{Po}$ form $\text{EO}_2$ and $\text{EO}_3$ type acidic oxides (True);
(B) Reducing property of dioxides decreases down Group 16, so $\text{SO}_2$ is reducing while $\text{TeO}_2$ is an oxidising agent (True);
(C) Reducing property of hydrides increases from $\text{H}_2\text{S}$ to $\text{H}_2\text{Te}$ down the group (False);
(D) Ozone ($\text{O}_3$) contains $6$ lone pairs of electrons, not $5$ (False).
Thus, A and B only.

Acidic oxides: $\text{Cl}_2\text{O}_7, \text{SiO}_2, \text{N}_2\text{O}_5$;
Neutral oxides: $\text{CO}, \text{NO}, \text{N}_2\text{O}$;
Amphoteric oxides: $\text{Al}_2\text{O}_3, \text{SnO}_2, \text{PbO}_2$ ($3$ oxides).

(A) Intermediate oxidation states ($+1$ to $+4$) of nitrogen disproportionate in acidic medium, e.g., $3\text{HNO}_2 \longrightarrow \text{HNO}_3 + \text{H}_2\text{O} + 2\text{NO}$ (Correct);
(B) Nitrogen lacks $d$-orbitals and forms $p\pi - p\pi$, not $d\pi - p\pi$, multiple bonds (Incorrect);
(C) $\text{N}-\text{N}$ single bond is weaker than $\text{P}-\text{P}$ single bond due to lone-pair repulsions (Incorrect);
(D) Nitrogen is a gas and has the lowest density in Group 15 (Incorrect);
(E) Nitrogen has only four valence orbitals ($2s$ and three $2p$), limiting its maximum covalency to four (Correct).
Thus, A and E Only.

(A) $\text{E}-\text{H}$ bond strength decreases down the group, so reducing character increases from $\text{NH}_3$ to $\text{BiH}_3$ (Correct);
(B) Electron density on the central atom decreases with increasing atomic size, so basicity decreases from $\text{NH}_3$ to $\text{BiH}_3$ (Correct);
(C) Thermal stability decreases from $\text{NH}_3$ to $\text{BiH}_3$ (Correct);
(D) As electronegativity of $\text{E}$ decreases down the group, bond pairs move farther from the central atom, reducing bond-pair–bond-pair repulsion and decreasing the $\text{H}-\text{E}-\text{H}$ bond angle ($\text{NH}_3: 107.8^\circ > \text{PH}_3: 93.6^\circ > \text{AsH}_3: 91.8^\circ > \text{SbH}_3: 91.3^\circ$) (Correct).
All statements A, B, C and D are correct.
